PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Split in round 0: 1/3/8 argue D (Weak Non-Sadism) via Sadistic Conclusion—CLU ranks some negative-welfare additions above sub-critical positive ones, directly negating the axiom while preserving the other four. 2/5/7 argue C (Non-Elitism) on the ground that a single supra-critical life can outrank arbitrarily many moderate positive lives. 4/6 argue E (Weak Quality Addition) because modest supra-critical additions can lower value relative to fewer high-welfare ones.  
Key factual claim to preserve: Arrhenius’s sixth theorem shows inconsistency among Egalitarian Dominance, General Non-Extreme Priority, Non-Elitism, Weak Non-Sadism, and Weak Quality Addition; each standard theory drops exactly one.  
My current belief: D is correct; CLU’s functional form sum(w_i − c) for c > 0 is known to entail the Sadistic Conclusion and therefore violates precisely Weak Non-Sadism. C and E appear to rest on mischaracterizations of the axioms or of how the critical-level shift affects them. Unresolved: need explicit statement of each axiom to confirm which one CLU actually falsifies.}

